; test_from_card.hasm -- a program whose own jump must be relocated to work.
;
; Stage 2B asks a question the loader cannot answer about itself: are the words
; in instruction memory right? There is no read port, so the only witness is the
; program. This one is built to be a sharp witness.
;
; Every small program that prints in this repository is straight-line -- no
; labels, so nothing to relocate, so running one proves the words arrived but
; not that the ADDRESSES inside them were fixed.
;
; THE LOOP IS CLOSED WITH `JMP`, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. Measured while
; writing this: `JNE` assembles to 0x24000FFD -- a RELATIVE offset of -3 -- so a
; conditional branch needs no relocation at all. `JMP` and `CALL` are the
; absolute ones (`PC <- IMM`, rtl/hcpu_pkg.vh), and they are what a relocation
; table is made of. That is also why the tables are small: 7.2 entries on
; average across the 41 programs that assemble.
;
; Built for 0x900, the `JMP` carries 0x901; loaded without relocation it would
; carry 0x001 and land in whatever sits there instead. So these three numbers
;
;   1
;   2
;   3
;
; only come out if the relocation was applied, and then it halts, which is what
; lets the wrapper report its cycle count.

        MOVI  R1, 0
loop:   ADDI  R1, R1, 1
        PRINT R1
        CMPI  R1, 3
        JEQ   done
        JMP   loop                  ; absolute: this is the relocated word
done:   HALT
